  "result": "Units mismatch. JWT `exp` = Unix seconds (~1.7B). `Date.now()` = milliseconds (~1.7T). So `Date.now() > token.exp` always true \u2014 every token \"valid.\"\n\n**Wrong:**\n```js\nif (Date.now() > token.exp) {\n  return next(new Error('Token expired'));\n}\n// Date.now() always > exp in seconds \u2014 rejects everything\n// OR if inverted: lets everything through\n```\n\n**Fix \u2014 divide by 1000:**\n```js\nconst nowSeconds = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);\nif (nowSeconds > token.exp) {\n  return next(new Error('Token expired'));\n}\nreturn next();\n```\n\nOr use a library that handles this: `jsonwebtoken.verify()` checks expiry automatically.",
